  <span class="lab" style="margin-top:40px">Why No One Has Done This Yet</span>
  <div class="nar">
   <p>Because it requires three things that rarely exist in one company: <strong>legal expertise</strong> to navigate ECTA, FICA, POPIA, and common law; <strong>operational excellence</strong> to train, vet, and manage human proxies at scale; and <strong>enterprise software capability</strong> to integrate into legacy banking, court, and municipal systems. Gig apps have the operations but not the legal depth or enterprise software. Law firms have the legal expertise but not the technology or scale. Software companies have the tech but not the human network or legal nuance. <strong>Presence is built to have all three.</strong></p>
  </div>

  <span class="lab" style="margin-top:30px">The Facts</span>
  <ul class="lst nar">
   <li><strong>ECTA validates electronic signatures.</strong> This has been law since 2002. It is not a loophole. It is the law.</li>
   <li><strong>Courts accept video-commissioned affidavits.</strong> This is not theoretical. It happens daily in South African courts.</li>
   <li><strong>The CCMA accepts video attendance as physical presence.</strong> This is codified in their amended rules.</li>
   <li><strong>Banks, dealerships, and employers already use digital signatures.</strong> Every car purchase, every employment contract, every credit card application proves this.</li>
   <li><strong>The diaspora is growing.</strong> Over one million South Africans live abroad. They need trusted local presence. They will pay for it.</li>
   <li><strong>Institutions are drowning in physical paperwork.</strong> They want to digitize. They need a trusted bridge.</li>
  </ul>

